## is 90 percent a fact about the corpus or about the selection
Almost certainly the selection: the rows here were chosen as the
instruments a live claim needs plus every instrument whose defect the
corpus records, and both populations are files whose authors were
paying attention. Checked rather than assumed, by splitting p4 own
per-file classification on whether the directory has a row here.

not_represented   220 of  735 state a control  (29.9%)
represented       206 of  398 state a control  (51.8%)

C4: the two groups must both be non-empty and must sum to p4 total,
or the split is dropping files.
p4 files: 1133

WHAT THIS DOES NOT SAY. It counts what the field claims, not what the
instrument did. A row saying a control fired is only as good as the
reading behind it, and four defects in this corpus were controls that
could not fail and would be counted here as fired.

--- appended by 192, reading this run against 185's ---

Same instrument, same controls, run over a probe.toml that has grown from 48
rows in 27 directories to 75 in 48. Nothing in the script changed; it is
committed at 185_probes/p8_the_rows_control_ratio.sh and this file is its
output on the larger input.

                        185's run        this run
  rows                        48              75
  represented set          75.0%           51.8%
  not_represented set      30.0%           29.9%

185 said its 90 percent was a fact about its selection rather than about the
corpus, and predicted the selection was the cause. That is now measured rather
than argued: the covered set fell 23 points toward the baseline as coverage
went from 27 directories to 48, and the uncovered set did not move at all.

The first pass chose the instruments a live claim needed AND the ones whose
defects the corpus records, and the second population is by construction the
work of authors who were paying attention. This pass had no such freedom: the
directories are whichever ones the 21 blocked claims happen to rest on, and
those are ordinary. 51.8 percent is what the corpus looks like when the
selection is made by what is blocked rather than by what is well built.
